      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n`vllm bench serve --plot-dataset-stats` finishes the requests but raises an `AssertionError` when used without another output option. Include dataset statistics plots when deciding whether to generate an output filename.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `--plot-dataset-stats` can produce its PNG without `--save-result`, `--append-result`, or `--plot-timeline`.\n- The plot respects `--result-dir` and `--result-filename`; saving a results JSON remains opt-in.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `uv run --offline --no-project --python .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/benchmarks/test_serve_cli.py -k dataset_stats_plot_without_saving_results -q`: **1 passed, 3 deselected**. The same regression test fails on the base commit.\n- Ran the actual benchmark CLI against a local deterministic OpenAI-compatible SSE fixture, using a cached tokenizer and two requests. Before: exit 1 at the filename assertion, no PNG. After: exit 0, one dataset statistics PNG, no results JSON. This was a CPU client/plotting check, without a model server.\n- `pre-commit run --files vllm/benchmarks/serve.py tests/benchmarks/test_serve_cli.py`: passed.\n\n## Details\n\n`main_async()` already handles dataset statistics plotting independently. The early return in `compute_result_filename()` omitted that flag. The change adds it to the existing condition and adds a CPU regression test to the CLI suite.\n\nI checked the open PR inventory and the complete diffs of 27 related `serve.py` PRs; none of the inspected changes fixes this filename condition.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
